{{Short description|Football tournament}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Play in Group F of the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]] began on 12 June and completed on 22 June 2006. [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] won the group and advanced to the round of 16, along with runners-up [[Australia men's national soccer team|Australia]]. [[Croatia national football team|Croatia]] and [[Japan national football team|Japan]] failed to advance.<ref>{{cite web |last=Saaid |first=Hamdan |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2006full.html |title=World Cup 2006 – Match Details |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=7 February 2007 |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> Australia's win against Japan was the first (and so far only) by a team from the [[Oceania Football Confederation]], having switched to the [[Asian Football Confederation]] after the tournament. It was also the only time that a team from the OFC had advanced to the second round of the tournament, as in [[1974 FIFA World Cup|1974]] Australia went out in the first round.

