===Brazil vs Croatia===
Brazil came into their opening match against Croatia as defending champions, having won their fifth World Cup at the [[ 2002 FIFA World Cup | 2002]] edition of the tournament, and were favourites to win the tournament.<ref >{{Cite web |website=BBC Sport |date=13 June 2006  |title=Brazil 1-0 Croatia |url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2006/4852868.stm}}</ref>

Just before half-time, [[Kaká|Kaká's]] curling left-footed strike put the Brazilians ahead. With the win, Brazil became the first team in World Cup history to win eight consecutive matches.<ref >{{Cite web |website=ABC News  | date=14 June 2006 |title=Kaka goal gives Brazil record-breaking win |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2006-06-14/kaka-goal-gives-brazil-record-breaking-win/1777674}}</ref>
