===Japan vs Croatia===
The last time the two sides met, Croatia defeated Japan [[1998 FIFA World Cup Group H#Japan vs Croatia|1–0]] in the [[1998 FIFA World Cup|1998 edition of the tournament]] in which Croatia went on to finish in third place.

With both teams having lost their opening fixtures, Croatian captain [[Niko Kovač]] told the [[Večernji List | Vecernji List]] that the fixture was “naše biti ili ne biti” (“our to be or not to be”),<ref name="Mackey">{{Cite web |last=Mackey |first=Rob | website=NY Times |date=18 June 2006 |title=FINAL: Japan 0 - Croatia 0 - The New York Times |url=https://archive.nytimes.com/worldcup.blogs.nytimes.com/2006/06/18/live-at-9-am-est-japan-vs-croatia/?eafs_enabled=false}}</ref> with the same outlet reporting for the Japanese the headline “Zico: Presing od prve minute” (“[[Zico (footballer)|Zico]]: Pressing from the first minute”).<ref name="Mackey"/>

Croatia's best opportunity to score came mid-way through the first half when [[Dado Pršo]] was fouled by defender [[Tsuneyasu Miyamoto]]. [[Darijo Srna]] stepped up to take the spot kick, but his strike was parried away by Japan goalkeeper [[Yoshikatsu Kawaguchi]].<ref >{{Cite web |website=ABC News |date=18 June 2006 |title=Croatia miss penalty in Japan stalemate |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2006-06-19/croatia-miss-penalty-in-japan-stalemate/1780826}}</ref>

