===Brazil vs Australia===
Both teams headed into the fixture having won their opening games. The two teams had met each other 7 times prior,<ref>{{Cite web |website=11v11 |title=Australia national football team: record v Brazil |url=https://www.11v11.com/teams/australia/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/Brazil/}}</ref> with their most recent game being a 1–0 win to Australia at the [[2001 FIFA Confederations Cup#Third place play-off | 2001 FIFA Confederations Cup]].

Australia's well-organised defence frustrated Brazil, who created only one opening in the first half when [[Ronaldo (Brazilian footballer)|Ronaldo]] flicked the ball over his head and into the path of [[Kaká]], whose shot went wide of Australia's goal.<ref name=Ingle>{{Cite web |last=Ingle | first=Sean |website=The Guardian |date=19 Jun 2006 |title=Brazil's luck makes up for a lack of fire |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2006/jun/19/worldcup2006.match4}}</ref> Early in the second half, striker [[Adriano (footballer, born February 1982)|Adriano]] put Brazil ahead with a low strike just outside the penalty box. Despite the setback, Australia pushed forward, with [[Harry Kewell]] volleying just over the Brazilian goal, and [[Mark Bresciano]] shooting via a [[bicycle kick]] which was saved by [[Dida (footballer, born 1973)|Dida]].<ref name=Ingle/>

Late in the second half, Brazil substitute [[Fred (footballer, born 1983)|Fred]] scored the second goal for Brazil via a rebound, and the game finished 2–0, securing Brazil's position to the [[2006 FIFA World Cup knockout stage|round of 16]].

After the final whistle, Harry Kewell complained to referee Markus Merk, alleging that he awarded Brazil so many free kicks that even the Brazilians became embarrassed.<ref >{{Cite web |website=Fox Sports |date=16 March 2017 |title=Harry Kewell on Shootout: Brazil ‘embarrassed’ v Australia at 2006 World Cup due to referee’s calls |url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/football/socceroos/harry-kewell-on-shootout-brazil-embarrassed-v-australia-at-2006-world-cup-due-to-referees-calls/news-story/07723e0018122b8c0914b27a2b94a19f}}</ref> FIFA subsequently commenced disciplinary procedures against Kewell, alleging that he repeatedly insulted Merk,<ref >{{Cite web |website=Socceroos |date=21 Jun 2006 |title=Kewell to face disciplinary hearing |url=https://socceroos.com.au/news/kewell-face-disciplinary-hearing}}</ref> but the disciplinary committee eventually cleared Kewell of any wrongdoing.<ref >{{Cite web |last=van Happen |first=Jan |date=21 Jun 2006 |title=Merk angers Fifa as Kewell is cleared of verbal abuse  |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2006/jun/21/worldcup2006.sport12 |website=The Guardian}}</ref>
